  You left out:
  - Easier mapping of normal unlit rooms
    - Fewer traps hit.
    - Less time for bad things to happen.
  - Mapping the mazes in Gehennom the hard way.
  - Seeing monsters at a greater distance for ranged attacks, avoidance,
    etc.

  Most of the benefits to a lit magic lamp are invisible. (pun
intended.)  When players on #nethack insisted on #rubbing their magic
lamps but didn't know what to wish for, I'd always recommend wishing for
a permanent light source.

  Wishing for some form of magic resistance early is good, but so are
poison resistance and reflection.  If it won't get you all three you'll
still be at risk.  A permanent light source simplifies a lot of the game
for me.

>I normally only rub magic lamps if i have more than one. With my track
>record, my choice is often that between a disappearing djinni and a
>permanent light source, and i can tell you the latter is a _lot_
